      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Local Utah Price Drivers"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Winter Weather Damage: Heavy snow loads and freeze-thaw cycles in regions like Park City or the Wasatch Front can compromise structural decking. If an inspector has to evaluate structural integrity or load capacity, fees will sit at the higher end.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6,
              7,
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Pitch & Height: Utah homes with steep pitches (common in high-snow areas to shed ice) increase risk. Multi-story homes add an extra $25 to $75 due to ladder safety logistics."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Square Footage: A standard 1,500 sq. ft. home sits near the low end of estimates, while homes exceeding 3,500 sq. ft. can push inspection costs up past $500."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Independent Inspectors vs. Roofing Contractors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roofing Companies: Local businesses like Vertex Roofing\nor A1 Roofing Utah\noften look at your roof for free. The trade-off is that these are typically sales visits intended to quote you for a repair or full replacement.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              9,
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Independent Certified Inspectors: They charge a flat diagnostic fee (usually $200 to $350) but give you an entirely unbiased assessment since they do not perform repair services themselves."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          11
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down your estimated fee, what is the approximate square footage of your home, and are you getting this inspection for routine maintenance or a real estate transaction?"
      }
